public class UtilityInvoice {
    public static int baseChargeCents(int days) {
        return days < 1 || days > 31 ? -1 : 500 + 20 * days;
    }

    public static int usageChargeCents(int units) {
        if (units < 0) {
            return -1;
        }
        int firstBlock = Math.min(units, 100);
        int extraBlock = Math.max(units - 100, 0);
        return 15 * firstBlock + 10 * extraBlock;
    }

    public static int serviceChargeCents(boolean paperBill) {
        return paperBill ? 80 : 0;
    }

    public static int totalCents(int days, int units, boolean paperBill) {
        int base = baseChargeCents(days);
        int usage = usageChargeCents(units);
        if (base < 0 || usage < 0) {
            return -1;
        }
        return base + usage + serviceChargeCents(paperBill);
    }
}

For 10 days and 120 units, baseChargeCents is 700 and usageChargeCents is 1700, so the paper-bill total is 2480. Each helper owns one rule, and totalCents composes their results.

