public class RecursiveDigits {
    public static int digitalRoot(int value) {
        long magnitude = value < 0 ? -(long) value : value;
        return reduce(magnitude);
    }

    private static int reduce(long value) {
        if (value < 10) {
            return (int) value;
        }
        return reduce(sumDigits(value));
    }

    private static long sumDigits(long value) {
        if (value < 10) {
            return value;
        }
        return value % 10 + sumDigits(value / 10);
    }
}

For 9875, sumDigits gives 29, then 11, then 2. The outer base case stops when the current value is a single digit.

The helper removes one decimal digit at every recursive call, and the long magnitude avoids the Integer.MIN_VALUE negation overflow.

