public static int[] rotateRight(int[] values, int shift) {
    if (values == null || values.length == 0) {
        return new int[0];
    }
    int n = values.length;
    int normalized = ((shift % n) + n) % n;
    int[] result = new int[n];
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        result[(i + normalized) % n] = values[i];
    }
    return result;
}

The stableUnique implementation remains a set plus an output list. rotateRight uses O(n) time and O(n) space, and the normalized shift makes negative values rotate left equivalently.

