## Idempotent Java request executor

Implement a self-contained Java request executor in a class named `RequestExecutor`.

### API contracts

The following declarations specify the required API.

```java
record WriteRequest(String body, String idempotencyKey) {}
enum TransportStatus { SUCCESS, TRANSIENT_FAILURE, PERMANENT_FAILURE, TIMEOUT }
record TransportResult(TransportStatus status, String response, String detail) {}
interface Transport { TransportResult send(WriteRequest request); }
interface RetryPolicy { boolean mayRetry(TransportResult failure, int failedAttempts); }
record StoredResult(String body, ExecutionResult result) {}
interface ResultStore { Optional<StoredResult> find(String key); void record(String key, StoredResult result); }
interface ExecutionResult {}
record SuccessResult(String response) implements ExecutionResult {}
record DefinitiveFailureResult(String detail) implements ExecutionResult {}
record UncertainResult(String detail) implements ExecutionResult {}
```

### [task][Implement safe request execution]()

- Define the supporting contracts in the submission: `WriteRequest`, `TransportStatus`, `TransportResult`, `Transport`, `RetryPolicy`, and `StoredResult` and `ResultStore`.
- Define a result hierarchy with `ExecutionResult`, `SuccessResult`, `DefinitiveFailureResult`, and `UncertainResult`.
- Expose `RequestExecutor(Transport transport, RetryPolicy retryPolicy, ResultStore resultStore)` and `ExecutionResult execute(String body, String idempotencyKey, int maxAttempts)`.
- Reject a null body, a blank key, or maxAttempts below one with `IllegalArgumentException`.
- Check ResultStore before the first transport call.
- On SUCCESS, return and record SuccessResult.
- A TRANSIENT_FAILURE may be retried only when RetryPolicy allows it and only until maxAttempts; an exhausted transient failure becomes a DefinitiveFailureResult.
- A PERMANENT_FAILURE is definitive and is never retried.
- If a TIMEOUT occurs after the remote service may have applied the write, return and record UncertainResult; never issue an unkeyed duplicate to resolve it.
- A later call with the same key and the same body must return the stored result with zero Transport calls; a same-key call with a different body must be rejected.
- Use only standard Java types and define every declaration needed to compile without a starter repository.
- Keep transport, retry decisions, and storage behind their interfaces.
- Store the original body together with every terminal result.
- On replay, compare bodies before returning the stored result; conflicting key reuse must throw `IllegalArgumentException`.

### [task][Check examples and boundary cases]()

- Test immediate success, one transient failure then success, exhausted retries, permanent rejection, timeout uncertainty, null and blank arguments, exact attempt counts, and safe replay with a recording Transport and ResultStore.
